DTEND:20260912T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:Become a Junior Ranger at Lake James State Park! Join a ranger 
 for a fun\, family-friendly hike along the ¾-mile Holly Discovery Trail a
 s we explore the forest and discover the plants\, animals\, and natural wo
 nders that make Lake James special.\n\nAlong the way\, participants will c
 omplete activities in the official Junior Ranger Activity Book\, which wil
 l be provided at the beginning of the program. After completing the activi
 ties\, each child will take the Junior Ranger pledge and be officially swo
 rn in as a Lake James State Park Junior Ranger.\n\nThis program is designe
 d for children and families. Wear comfortable walking shoes\, bring water\
 , and be prepared to spend the hour outdoors.
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park - Paddy's Creek Access\, Holly Discovery Tra
 il
SUMMARY:Junior Ranger Adventure
