DESCRIPTION:In celebration of America’s 250th anniversary\, the Black Pat
 riots Commemoration Project\, in collaboration with the International Civi
 l Rights Center & Museum\, presents Unsung Heroes: Black Patriots of the R
 evolution.\n\nThis program highlights often-overlooked African Americans w
 ho\, in pursuit of freedom\, helped shape American independence.\n\nThroug
 h performance\, film\, interpretation\, and conversation\, the weekend con
 nects their stories and the ideals of the American Revolution to the Ameri
 can story.\n\nSponsored in part by America250 Guilford County\n\n1:00 pm -
  2:00 pm - "Black Patriots" film by Kareem Abdul-Jabbar\n\n2:00 pm - 4:00 
 pm - Guided Bus Tour at Guilford Courthouse National Military Park
GEO:36.071722;-79.790579
LOCATION:International Civil Rights Center and Museum
SUMMARY:Unsung Heroes: Black Patriots of the Revolution - Film and Guided B
 us Tour
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/unsung-heroes-black-patriots
 -of-the-revolution-film-and-guided-bus-tour
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
