DESCRIPTION:The African American Cultural Center (AACC) Library Reader Loun
 ge is a monthly silent book club and communal reading session that allows 
 students\, faculty and staff to connect over a shared love for books and r
 ead in a relaxed\, social atmosphere. Meet new friends\, share thoughts on
  your current read and discover new titles from our specialized collection
  on African-American and Afro-diasporic experiences\, culture\, society an
 d history.\n\n You can bring your own book\, explore the shelves for your 
 next read\, ask the AACC Librarians for a curated suggestion or pick up a 
 mystery book to read. You can even bring your reading assignments if you l
 ike. Come solo or bring your friends. All are welcome to join. There will 
 be:\n\nEndless books to choose fromCommunity introductions and book recomm
 endationsSnacks\, tea and coffeeBookish prizesCozy spaces and blanketsSpac
 e to discuss your chosen book and share your book review with your new fri
 ends
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (218
 )
