BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ackland Art Museum": "https://events.ackland.org/event/she-will-be-quite-a-manager-from-plantation-owner-to-girl-boss/", "UNC Chapel Hill": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/she-will-be-quite-a-manager-from-plantation-owner-to-girl-boss"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.ackland.org/event/she-will-be-quite-a-manager-from-plantation-owner-to-girl-boss/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
X-SOURCE:Ackland Art Museum, UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T190000
DTSTAMP:20260825T173423Z
CREATED:20260825T173423Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260825T173423Z
UID:10004469-1789666200-1789671600@events.ackland.org
SUMMARY:“She Will Be Quite a Manager”: From Plantation Owner to Girl Boss
DESCRIPTION:What do a Civil War-era plantation owner and a modern “girl boss” have in common? More than you think. \nAdelicia Acklen and Dorothy Thomas were two of the most powerful plantation-owning women—one in the US South and the other in South America—but both wielded the power of ownership by deploying and playing on particular ideas of femininity. This talk hosted by Carolina Public Humanities traces their unsettling legacy into the present\, asking what happens when women gain power within systems built on inequality. \nFree\, but space is limited; registration is required via the Carolina Public Humanities event webpage. \nAbout the speaker: \nTanya Shields is an Associate Professor of Women’s and Gender Studies whose research focuses on Caribbean studies and plantation logics. She teaches courses on the Caribbean\, the arts of activism\, growing up girls globally\, and the continuing influence of plantation economics and politics. She is currently working on her second monograph\, Gendered Labor: Race\, Place\, and Power on Female-Owned Plantations\, a comparative study of women who owned plantations in the Caribbean and the U.S. South. \n  \n 
URL:https://events.ackland.org/event/she-will-be-quite-a-manager-from-plantation-owner-to-girl-boss/
LOCATION:Ackland Art Museum\, 101 S. Columbia Street\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:Talks
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.ackland.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-25-133013.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Cloud Security Alliance Triangle Chapter": "https://www.meetup.com/cloud-security-alliance-triangle-chapter/events/316314126/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_cloud_security_alliance_triangle_chapter
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Cloud Security Alliance Triangle
UID:event_316314126@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260913T043359Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T200000
SUMMARY:From Passwords to Prompts: Evolving Identity Governance for the Ag
 entic Era
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Security Alliance Triangle Chapter\n**Summary of Present
 ation:** Identity resilience has long meant protecting accounts\, governin
 g access\, and recovering from breach—but the definition of “identity
 ” has changed. AI agents are already inside your enterprise\, booking me
 etings\, processing invoices\, querying databases\, calling APIs\, and mak
 ing autonomous decisions\, all without the usernames and passwords your tr
 aditional IAM stack was built to manage. They authenticate via OAuth token
 s\, API keys\, service accounts\, and MCP connections\, are provisioned qu
 ickly\, documented poorly\, and are often governed not at all. When one is
  compromised\, the blast radius can dwarf a human account breach.\nThe ses
 sion draws on a year of running AI agents in production for podcast bookin
 g\, content editing\, and publishing worlows\, combined with more than two
  decades of identity experience at SailPoint\, AWS\, and Saviynt\, to map 
 what’s actually breaking and how to fix it. Attendees will come away wit
 h a clear framework for extending IGA\, PAM\, and Zero Trust programs to c
 over non-human and agentic identities—what to inventory\, how to scope e
 ntitlements\, where lateral movement risk hides in your agent mesh\, and w
 hat true resilience looks like when half your “workforce” never logs i
 n.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/cloud-security-alliance-triangle-chap
 ter/events/316314126/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260828T162455Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260828T162455Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
