UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53798217063455
DTSTART:20260922T210000Z
DTEND:20260922T223000Z
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of National Forensic Science Week 2026\, what ex
 actly is forensic science\, and how is it used in the real world? Join us 
 for an introduction to the science behind forensic investigations and expl
 ore the many ways forensic science is applied to analyze evidence and supp
 ort investigations and put your forensic science skills to the test in thi
 s interactive case investigation! During this event\, you’ll be presente
 d with the details of a fictional case and challenged to work alongside th
 e people around you to evaluate key aspects of the investigation and piece
  together what happened. As the case unfolds\, you’ll tackle different f
 orensic science questions\, discuss your findings with your team\, and use
  critical thinking and collaboration to work toward a final conclusion. Ca
 n you work the case and figure out what happened? Join us for Let’s Work
  a Case and find out!
GEO:35.908258;-79.050937
LOCATION:Coker Hall\, 215
SUMMARY:Let's Work a Case
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/lets-work-a-case
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/unc-postdoctoral-associations-research-cafe-5289"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260913T043500Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53932405369416
DTSTART:20260922T220000Z
DTEND:20260922T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:Every day\, the blood in our bodies performs an extraordinary b
 alancing act: flowing freely through our vessels when we are healthy\, yet
  rapidly forming clots when we are injured to prevent dangerous blood loss
 . But how does the body know when to switch from flowing to clotting? Join
  this installation of Research Cafe to hear Dr. Yuriy Prokopenko\, MD\, an
  expert in hemophilia\, tell us about this remarkable process and how hemo
 philia affects it. In this talk\, Dr. Prokopenko will offer his perspectiv
 es on clinical diagnosis\, advances in modern treatment\, as well as the e
 xciting contributions Carolina scientists have made to hemophilia. Join us
  on Tuesday\, September 22nd\, from 6:00 – 7:00 PM at the Chapel Hill Pu
 blic Library to learn about blood and hemophilia. Light refreshment will b
 e provided
GEO:35.932032;-79.035632
LOCATION:Chapel Hill Public Library\, Meeting Room A
SUMMARY:UNC Postdoctoral Association's Research Cafe
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/unc-postdoctoral-associations-
 research-cafe-5289
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
