DESCRIPTION:Join a Park Ranger and learn why the trees change color! Which 
 tree keeps its leaves all winter? If chlorophyll makes leaves green\, what
  makes green leaves become other colors? Learn the answers to these questi
 ons and tips for Winter Tree Identification during the hike at the Histori
 c Occoneechee Speedway.\n\nAll children must be accompanied by an adult. P
 lease be sure to dress appropriately for the weather\, wear hiking shoes\,
  and bring water!\n\nSpaces are limited\, and registration is required. To
  sign up\, call (984) 250-1370 or email eno.river@ncparks.gov. Include the
  number of guests in your party and a phone number where you can be reache
 d if the event is changed or canceled.
GEO:36.069875;-79.085451
LOCATION:Eno River State Park - Occoneechee Speedway Access\, Parking Lot
SUMMARY:Changing Leaves Tree ID Hike
