DESCRIPTION:<p>Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Saturday 
 from 10am-11:30am with signs to protect our democracy and protest the viol
 ations to our Constitution. We will meet at the YMCA at 218 West Morgan St
 .</p><p>We need to fight for our democracy and stop and prevent future cut
 s that are hurting many. Bring friends! Bring signs that show your concern
  or are a call to action. Please avoid triggering images like swastikas.</
 p><p>See you every Saturday morning engaging drivers &amp\; pedestrians in
  Downtown Durham!</p><p>Please join our Substack:<span> </span><a href="h
 ttps://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy">https
 ://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy</a></p><p>
 For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<span> </span><a href="https://www.mobilize
 .us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersf
 ordemocracy/</a></p><p><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfor
 democracy/event/842514/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocra
 cy/event/842514/</a> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260108T021307Z
LOCATION:218 W Morgan St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Moreheadplanetarium": "https://moreheadplanetarium.org/calendar/saturday-science-sparks-sept2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:moreheadplanetarium
X-SOURCE:Morehead Planetarium & Science Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260926T150000
DTSTAMP:20260913T003409
CREATED:20260612T185410Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260910T172421Z
UID:39788-1790416800-1790434800@moreheadplanetarium.org
SUMMARY:Saturday Science Sparks: The Science of Sea Turtles
DESCRIPTION:The Science of Sea Turtles\n\n\n\nThis September\, navigate to Morehead to meet scientists from the UNC Department of Biology Lohmann Lab! As they spotlight their latest research\, get hands-on with biology\, physics\, and engineering while we look at nature’s best navigators and explore how marine animals make their way in the world.  \n\n\n\nMORE is happening at Morehead this year\n\n\n\nNew for 2026\, Saturday Science Sparks offers Morehead guests a closer encounter with current science. Covering topics like astronomy\, the physics of juggling\, and computer science\, this program collaborates with community partners and academic clubs\, bringing you up-close experiences in the exciting world of STEAM. Saturday Science Sparks is open to the public and included in admission.
URL:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/calendar/saturday-science-sparks-sept2026/
LOCATION:Morehead Planetarium and Science Center\, 250 E Franklin St\, Chapel Hill\, North Carolina\, 27516\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/olga-ga-iRgbLpf50IE-unsplash-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
