DESCRIPTION:Become a FrogWatch USA volunteer with the NC Aquariums Chapter.
  The 2-day volunteer training\, hosted by Crowders Mountain State Park is 
 being offered on September 26 (10:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m.) and September 27 (1
 :00 p.m. - 4:00 p.m.). Become a FrogWatch USA community scientist by atten
 ding both dates.\n\nFrogWatch USA volunteers learn to identify frogs and t
 oads by their breeding calls. Each 2-day training introduces FrogWatch pro
 tocols and procedures\, introduces the breeding calls of local species\, a
 nd provides a mock listening sessions for practice. Volunteers who complet
 e the training are invited to engage in social listening sessions througho
 ut southeast NC and receive a quarterly newsletter regarding FrogWatch act
 ivity.\n\n(To register or to see other training dates/locations\, please v
 isit the NC Aquarium at Fort Fisher website at the link provided. For more
  information about FrogWatch USA and becoming a volunteer\, please email K
 ristin.Holloman-Noe@ncaquariums.com.
GEO:35.212572;-81.292771
LOCATION:Crowders Mountain State Park\, Visitor Center
SUMMARY:NC Aquariums Chapter of FrogWatch USA volunteer training
