DESCRIPTION:Join us at Mayo River State Park for a Harvest Moon Hike!\n\nTh
 e Harvest Moon is the full moon of the Fall Equinox and named after the pe
 ak harvesting season for farmers\, as the brightness would extend the harv
 esting days. We encourage you to come join us in celebration of the beginn
 ing of the fall season as we hike along the Fox Trail\, an easy-moderate 2
  mile hike\, through the peaceful foliage of the Mayo Mountain area. \n\nP
 lease bring water\, hiking shoes\, and flashlights.\n\nEvent is subject to
  cancel due to poor weather. Please click the "I'm Interested" button as e
 vent will cancel when there are no registrations and recieve emails if can
 celed due to weather.
GEO:36.439192;-79.948638
LOCATION:Mayo River State Park - Main Access and Park Office
