DESCRIPTION:*Registration required to reserve your spot* Follow the link to
  reserve your spot.        The registration link will be available startin
 g 9/17/26.\n\nJoin a Lake James State Park Ranger for a relaxing morning b
 oat tour on beautiful Lake James! Participants will enjoy approximately tw
 o hours on the water while exploring the lake and learning about its fasci
 nating history and natural resources. As we cruise along the shoreline\, w
 e will keep our eyes open for wildlife\, waterfowl\, and Bald Eagles. This
  will be an opportunity to experience Lake James State Park from a differe
 nt perspective.\n\nMeeting Location: Lake James State Park Paddy's Creek A
 ccess- East Shelter\nDuration: Approximately 2 hours 8:00AM-10:00AM\n\nPle
 ase Bring: Personal floatation device(we can provide basic PFDs if needed)
 \, water\, sunglasses\n\nThings to know: Participants may bring cameras or
  other items they feel will make them comfortable but please pack light as
  space will be limited on the boat. Everybody must register prior to the e
 vent to have a spot on the boat. Registration is only for the name listed\
 , children or spouses have to register separately. Space is limited to 6 p
 eople. If you cannot make it please call us so we can open the spot for an
 other person.
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park - Paddy's Creek Access\, East Shelter
SUMMARY:Morning Lake Discovery Tour 
