END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:Defend Democracy Saturdays: Downtown Durham
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T113000
DTSTAMP:20260913T043349Z
UID:7vihpmeg1k6esqp5s5vsvq9hfe_R20260110T150000@google.com__20261003
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20251010T141601Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Saturday 
 from 10am-11:30am with signs to protect our democracy and protest the viol
 ations to our Constitution. We will meet at the YMCA at 218 West Morgan St
 .</p><p>We need to fight for our democracy and stop and prevent future cut
 s that are hurting many. Bring friends! Bring signs that show your concern
  or are a call to action. Please avoid triggering images like swastikas.</
 p><p>See you every Saturday morning engaging drivers &amp\; pedestrians in
  Downtown Durham!</p><p>Please join our Substack:<span> </span><a href="h
 ttps://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy">https
 ://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy</a></p><p>
 For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<span> </span><a href="https://www.mobilize
 .us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersf
 ordemocracy/</a></p><p><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfor
 democracy/event/842514/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocra
 cy/event/842514/</a> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260108T021307Z
LOCATION:218 W Morgan St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardens": "https://gardens.duke.edu/event/japanese-tea-gathering-kanna-zuki-1st-seating/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardens
X-SOURCE:Sarah P. Duke Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T114500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T131500
DTSTAMP:20260908T195240Z
CREATED:20260908T195240Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260908T195240Z
UID:17879-1791027900-1791033300@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:Japanese Tea Gathering: Kanna-zuki -1st seating
DESCRIPTION:Join tea master Chizuko Sueyoshi and members of the Japanese Tea Practitioners of Durham for a moment of respite in the Duke Gardens teahouse\, where you will experience the centering calm of a Japanese tea gathering in the Urasenke tradition. Enjoy the aesthetics\, poetry and serenity of this rich tradition over an enticing bowl of whisked green tea and a Japanese confection.  Guests will be escorted on a 15-minute walk to the teahouse\, where seating is on the floor unless a chair is requested upon registration by emailing GardensEducation@duke.edu. For ages 12 and up. \nFee: $68; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Fees apply \nLocation: Onsite at Duke Gardens. \nAccessibility: This is a small group program that takes place indoors in a non-climate controlled space with floor seating\, in a location that requires outdoors traveling on a combination of paved and unpaved paths with some uneven surfaces and moderate inclines.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/japanese-tea-gathering-kanna-zuki-1st-seating/
LOCATION:Onsite at Duke Gardens – directions to follow
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs,Tea Ceremony
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Growing-2024-Transformations-AFTER-Tea-House-Brian-Wells-2018.jpg
END:VEVENT
