X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/carolina-science-cafe-whos-a-journalist-in-the-age-of-ai"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260913T043501Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53887564818928
DTSTART:20261006T220000Z
DTEND:20261006T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:Who’s a Journalist in the Age of AI?\n\nTheorizing Distribute
 d Journalistic Authority Amid Newsfluencers\, Algorithms\, and Generative 
 Systems\n\n \n\nWho’s a Journalist in the Age of AI? addresses a critica
 l development in the news media. In this talk\, UNC-Chapel Hill’s Hussma
 n School of Journalism and Media faculty member\, Deb Aikat\, PhD\, will d
 iscuss how generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) reconfigures the epi
 stemic boundaries of journalistic authority\, credibility\, and public ver
 ification in democratic discourse.\n\n \n\nDr. Aikat will discuss how AI i
 s reshaping press freedom at a time when public trust in media has sunk to
  28%\, according to Gallup’s 2025 survey. He studies the shifting inform
 ation landscape in the U.S. and India — the world’s oldest and largest
  democracies — tracing how digital platforms empower people to publish\,
  protest\, and participate in civic life beyond traditional newsrooms.\n\n
  \n\nCarolina Science Cafe is a free program by Morehead Planetarium and S
 cience Center that explores current science topics making headlines. This 
 special program is hosted at Haw River Tap & Table in Carrboro on the firs
 t Tuesday of every month. Light appetizers are available for all attendees
 .
GEO:35.910154;-79.068833
LOCATION:Haw River Tap & Table
SUMMARY:Carolina Science Cafe: Who’s a Journalist in the Age of AI?
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/carolina-science-cafe-whos-a-j
 ournalist-in-the-age-of-ai
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
