UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53578446342426
DTSTART:20261008T170000Z
DTEND:20261008T183000Z
DESCRIPTION:This beginner-friendly workshop is designed to help you build c
 onfidence with version control and collaborative coding. In this session\,
  you’ll learn the basics of Git\, including how to track changes\, manag
 e project history\, and recover earlier versions of your work. You’ll al
 so explore GitHub\, a platform built on Git\, which allows code sharing\, 
 collaboration\, and project organization. You will leave with a practical 
 understanding of key concepts and the skills to start using Git and GitHub
  in your own work.\n\n \n\nNo prior experience with Git or GitHub is requi
 red. This workshop is ideal for anyone working on research projects\, digi
 tal humanities\, data analysis\, or software development.\n\n \n\nThis wor
 kshop is offered by the University Library and will be led by librarians M
 att Jansen and Rolando Rodriguez. \n\n \n\nThis workshop is being offered 
 remotely via Zoom. Register here: https://calendar.lib.unc.edu/event/17236
 848
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Introduction to Git and GitHub
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-git-and-github
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
