BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/agentic-ai-8711"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260913T043501Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53797539117044
DTSTART:20261008T180000Z
DTEND:20261008T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Want to do more with AI? Agents can help. AI agents are designe
 d to work toward specific goals and complete tasks with less step-by-step 
 direction from the user. While they can be powerful and efficient tools\, 
 giving them too much autonomy can also create problems. In this workshop\,
  you’ll learn what AI agents can do\, where their limits are\, and how t
 o create and use your own using the UNC Library’s PromptLab. No prior ex
 perience with agents is required\, though participants who are new to gene
 rative AI may find it helpful to review our brief training videos before t
 aking this workshop.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the University Li
 braries and will be led by librarian Michele Hayslett.\n\n \n\nThis worksh
 op is being offered remotely via Zoom only. You can register through the l
 ibrary calendar. Registrants will receive a Zoom link\; those on the waitl
 ist will not receive a Zoom link unless they are bumped up to a registered
  spot.\n\n\nAll registrants however\, will receive access to the meeting r
 ecording and resources.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Agentic AI
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/agentic-ai-8711
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
