BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardens": "https://gardens.duke.edu/event/climate-up-close/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardens
X-SOURCE:Sarah P. Duke Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T151500
DTSTAMP:20260908T195008Z
CREATED:20260908T195008Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260908T195008Z
UID:17877-1791727200-1791731700@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:Climate Up Close
DESCRIPTION:Meet a panel of climate scientists\, including Dr. Nadir Jeevanjee (NOAA)\, Dr. Aaron Match (Cornell University)\, Dr. Nathaniel Tarshish (Harvard University) and Dr. Andrew Williams (Princeton University)\, to explore the known and unknown of climate science with a brief presentation and plenty of time for questions and discussion. Climate Up Close is a group of climate scientists committed to making the essentials of climate science accessible to a broad audience. They share what they know to equip Americans to reach their own judgments about climate science by seeing the evidence for themselves and putting their questions directly to climate scientists. Climate Up Close is non-partisan and non-prescriptive. \nFee: Free; registration encouraged. \nParking: Parking fees apply.\n \nLocation: Pelham-Cullen Classroom inside the Barnes Welcome Center.\n \nAccessibility: This program takes place seated in an indoor location accessible via paved surfaces and equipped with a hearing loop\, which transmits sound directly to hearing aids and cochlear implants with a T-coil setting. Accessible restrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/climate-up-close/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Pelham-Cullen Classroom in the Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Hanley_Doris-Duke-Gardens_tree-and-bench_6-5-21-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
