DTSTART:20261016T230000Z
DTEND:20261017T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Vance Birthplace on Friday\, Oct. 16 to get into the
  spirit of Halloween with spooky stories from Appalachia and beyond! Dr. D
 elanna Reed\, professor emerita of Storytelling at East Tennessee State Un
 iversity\, will bring these tales to life through spoken word from 7pm to 
 8pm. Visitors are welcome to bring a blanket or chair\, and as the sun set
 s\, they can take a seat around our campfire. These stories are suitable f
 or ages 12 and up.\n\nThis event is free and does not require registration
  in advance\, but donations are encouraged. If you have any questions\, pl
 ease reach out via email at vance@dncr.nc.gov or by phone at (828) 645-670
 6!
GEO:35.700986;-82.496251
LOCATION:Governor Zebulon B. Vance Birthplace
SUMMARY:Frightful Folk Tales at Vance Birthplace
