DTSTAMP:20260913T043427Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53496819586736
DTSTART:20261024T130000Z
DTEND:20261024T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Prepare\, pin and mount a variety of spectacular tropical butte
 rflies. Learn the various techniques used to catch\, preserve and mount th
 ese and other fascinating arthropods. Explore the possibilities of insect 
 collecting in your backyard.\n\nCredit: 3 contact hours toward CEUs or Cri
 teria III for North Carolina’s Environmental Education Certification Pro
 gram\nUpon completion of the Trek\, you will receive a Certificate of Cour
 se Completion that includes the number of contact hours to turn in for CEU
 s. For those seeking Environmental Education Certification\, you will also
  receive an EE Form for up to 3 hours of credit.\n\nRegistration: Register
  here online\nThe full workshop fee is due when you register and payment i
 s via credit card. Registration for most Educator Treks is on a first-come
 \, first-served basis. Treks fill quickly\, so register early!\n\nProgram 
 Details:\n\nFee: $70* (includes insect resource manual\, pinning board\, b
 utterfly display box\, numerous exotic butterfly specimens)Requirements: F
 or educators (includes teachers\, administrators\, pre-service or substitu
 te teachers\; non-formal educators\; anyone working on their EE certificat
 ion)Program Instructor(s): Andy Kauffman\, Colin BrammerActivity Level: Ea
 sy: Workshop will take place indoors in a lab settingCategories: Educator 
 Treks\, Educators\, WorkshopsNote: We do not want cost to be a barrier for
  any educator. If the cost of this workshop would prevent your participati
 on\, please reach out to Megan Davis.
GEO:35.782138;-78.641055
LOCATION:NC Museum of Natural Sciences: Nature Research Center
SUMMARY:Educator Trek: Butterfly Pinning and Backyard Bug Collecting
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/educator-trek-butterfly-pinn
 ing-and-backyard-bug-collecting
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-nation-the-fight-for-independence"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260913T043427Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53312428123607
DTSTART:20261024T140000Z
DTEND:20261024T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Catawba Cultural Center\, Kings Mountai
 n Historical Museum is excited to present\, "Choosing Sides: The Catawba N
 ation & the Fight for Independence." This exhibit explores the critical ro
 le of the Catawba Nation\, also known as Yį Iswąre or “People of the R
 iver\,” in the American Revolutionary War\, particularly in the backcoun
 try regions of Tryon and Lincoln Counties. As skilled warriors\, guides\, 
 and allies of the Patriot cause\, the Catawba people defended their homela
 nd\, protected settler communities\, and contributed to pivotal battles. D
 espite the hardships of disease\, displacement\, and warfare\, the Catawba
  demonstrated extraordinary resilience. Their story is one of courage\, al
 liance\, and survival\, woven into the struggle for independence in the So
 uthern Campaign of the Revolution.\n\nThe exhibit will run from June 30\, 
 2026 until October 24\, 2026. Admission is Free!
GEO:35.239004;-81.342181
LOCATION:Kings Mountain Historical Museum
SUMMARY:Choosing Sides: The Catawba Nation & The Fight for Independence
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-n
 ation-the-fight-for-independence
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining-north-carolinas-black-heritage"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260913T043427Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53138241989665
DTSTART:20261024T140000Z
DTEND:20261024T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
  at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design presents a series of vignettes explor
 ing spaces of dignity\, belonging\, safety\, and imagination within Black 
 communities across North Carolina. Featuring historical photographs\, cont
 emporary images\, artworks from the Gregg Museum collection including a ha
 ndmade guitar by Freeman Vines\, and ephemera from community partners\, th
 e exhibition reflects on place\, memory\, creativity\, and spiritual resil
 ience across generations. Through stories of triumph and adversity\, Commu
 nity Stories honors the ways Black Americans have sustained and uplifted t
 heir communities through family\, entrepreneurship\, cultural expression\,
  and soulful imagination\, while inspiring future generations.
GEO:35.784925;-78.661662
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining
 -north-carolinas-black-heritage
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
