BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/the-battle-of-shallow-ford-an-exhibition-of-watercolors-and-words"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260913T043427Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53876935876763
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DESCRIPTION:On Display September 3 – Octobe 30\, 2026\n\nThis collection 
 of “watercolors” by master craftsman Rick Jones is accompanied by stor
 yboards of “words” by artist and writer\, Marilyn Ingram. The story\, 
 unfolding during a time where there were no cameras\, cell phones\, or eve
 n a typewriter\, is told through the eyes of artists\, field correspondent
 s who would paint\, draw or write a journal. The paintings include scenes 
 at the Shallow Ford and nearby battle area\, Moravian settlements along th
 e great wagon road\, and annual commemoration in Huntsville\, NC. The word
 s are researched through works including “Records of the Moravians” an
 d NC State Archives. This exhibition is presented in partnership with The 
 Lewisville Area Arts Council and was supported by the America 250 NC Commu
 nity Grant.\n\n \n\nAn opening reception will be held September 3 from 5-7
 pm at the Yadkin Cultural Arts Center.\n\nRefreshments will be served.\n\n
 Free Admission\, all are welcome to attend.\n\n**There will be a second ce
 lebration of this exhibit on Friday\, October 9 (5-7pm) in honor of the 24
 6th Commemoration Weekend of this historical event.**
LOCATION:Welborn Gallery
SUMMARY:The Battle of Shallow Ford: An Exhibition of Watercolors and Words 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/the-battle-of-shallow-ford-a
 n-exhibition-of-watercolors-and-words
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
END:VEVENT
