DTEND:20261103T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Located at the Park’s Visitor Center\, the newly established 
 Native Landscape Garden's mission is to teach visitors to the park about n
 ative plants and their importance as well as the native pollinator species
  that rely on them. On the first Tuesday of each month\, beginning July 7 
 and continuing through November 3\, join Park Rangers to perform maintenan
 ce on the gardens so they continue to serve as a living native plant educa
 tion opportunity to all who view them. Bring work gloves\, water\, hats an
 d weather-appropriate clothing. Volunteers will receive a Friends of Gorge
 s State Park Volunteer T-Shirt. For more information or to sign up\, go to
  https://www.signupgenius.com/go/10C0B4CAAAC28A5FAC25-64387146-native
GEO:35.096282;-82.950567
LOCATION:Gorges State Park - Grassy Ridge Access & Visitor Center\, Visitor
  Center
SUMMARY:Native Plant Gardens Volunteer Day - NC the Beautiful
