DTSTART:20261105T223000Z
DTEND:20261106T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Department of Art and Art History\n\n \n\nSheida Soleimani is a
 n Iranian-American artist who lives in Providence. The daughter of politic
 al refugees who were persecuted by the Iranian government in the early 198
 0s\, Soleimani makes work that melds sculpture\, collage and photography a
 nd highlights her own critical perspective on historical and contemporary 
 socio-political occurrences in Iran. She focuses on media trends and the d
 issemination of societal occurrences in the news\, adapting images from po
 pular press and social media leaks to exist within alternate scenarios. He
 r work has been recognized internationally in both exhibitions and publica
 tions such as Artforum\, The New York Times\, The Huffington Post\, Interv
 iew\, and VICE Magazine.\n\n \n\nSoleimani is an Associate Professor of Fi
 ne Arts at Brandeis University and a 2026 Guggenheim Fellow.\n\n \n\nAn en
 dowment established in 1983 through the generosity of Nancy and Robin Hane
 s supports the Art Department's Visiting Artist Series. This important pro
 gram brings both established and emerging artists to campus to discuss the
 ir work in public lectures and to offer individual critiques to our M.F.A.
  students.  The Hanes Visiting Artist series greatly enriches both our aca
 demic programs and our outreach to the wider community.  All lectures are 
 free and open to the public.\n\n \n\nA weeknight or daytime permit is now 
 required after 5:00 pm on weekdays. No permit is required from 5:00 pm Fri
 day through 7:30 am Monday. A $1.00 one-night pass is available in selecte
 d lots. More information can be found HERE.\n\nSheida Soleimani is an Iran
 ian-American artist who lives in Providence. The daughter of political ref
 ugees who were persecuted by the Iranian government in the early 1980s\, S
 oleimani makes work that melds sculpture\, collage and photography and hig
 hlights her own critical perspective on historical and contemporary socio-
 political occurrences in Iran. She focuses on media trends and the dissemi
 nation of societal occurrences in the news\, adapting images from popular 
 press and social media leaks to exist within alternate scenarios. Her work
  has been recognized internationally in both exhibitions and publications 
 such as Artforum\, The New York Times\, The Huffington Post\, Interview\, 
 and VICE Magazine.\n\n \n\nSoleimani is an Associate Professor of Fine Art
 s at Brandeis University and a 2026 Guggenheim Fellow.\n\n \n\nAn endowmen
 t established in 1983 through the generosity of Nancy and Robin Hanes supp
 orts the Art Department's Visiting Artist Series. This important program b
 rings both established and emerging artists to campus to discuss their wor
 k in public lectures and to offer individual critiques to our M.F.A. stude
 nts.  The Hanes Visiting Artist series greatly enriches both our academic 
 programs and our outreach to the wider community.  All lectures are free a
 nd open to the public.\n\n \n\nA weeknight or daytime permit is now requir
 ed after 5:00 pm on weekdays. No permit is required from 5:00 pm Friday th
 rough 7:30 am Monday. A $1.00 one-night pass is available in selected lots
 . More information can be found HERE.\n\n \n\nContact: Martin Wannam\, mwa
 nna@unc.edu
GEO:35.91175;-79.048576
LOCATION:Hamilton Hall\, 100
SUMMARY:Hanes Visiting Artist Lecture Series: Sheida Soleimani
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/hanes-visiting-artist-lecture-
 series-sheida-soleimani
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
