DTSTAMP:20260913T043431Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53320897836258
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270117
DESCRIPTION:Applications for the 2027 Mexico’s Magical Migrations Institu
 te are now open.\n\nExperience one of the world’s greatest migrations: m
 onarch butterflies on their wintering grounds.Observe humpback whale socia
 l interactions.Visit and learn about the Mazahua people at La Casa de la C
 ultura Mazahua.Discover connections between Mexico and North Carolina.Part
 icipating educators will witness two of nature’s greatest spectacles –
  wintering monarch butterflies and humpback whales. Each year one of the w
 orld’s greatest migrations takes place as millions of monarch butterflie
 s from the US and Canada travel south to the forested Mexican highlands. O
 nce they arrive\, they begin a period of winter hibernation by clustering 
 together in huge numbers\, blanketing the surrounding vegetation. As the b
 utterflies are arriving in Mexico\, so are humpback whales. Concluding the
 ir own incredible migration from their feeding waters off Alaska\, large n
 umbers of humpback whales gather off Mexico’s Pacific coast. They come t
 o these warmer waters to breed and to give birth. Learn about these magica
 l migrations from local experts and explore connections to North Carolina.
  We will share our adventures with students at home through daily blog pos
 ts from the field.\n\nDates: January 13-20\, 2027. (Mandatory pre- and pos
 t-trip sessions will be held in Raleigh on Saturday\, December 5\, 2026 an
 d Saturday\, November 6\, 2027.)\n\nLocations: Toluca\, Macho de Agua\, an
 d Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico and Raleigh\, N.C.\n\nGroup Size: Limited to 12
  participants. (Note: We anticipate that Mexican teachers will join with A
 merican educators to form an international team.)\n\nActivity Level: Moder
 ate to rigorous including hiking (up to 2 miles) on uneven terrain\, walki
 ng at high altitudes (~10\,000 ft)\, and riding horses on trails with a gu
 ide.\n\nCost: $2200*\nIncludes round-trip airfare from Raleigh to Mexico\,
  in-country transportation\, instruction\, lodging\, and meals. Participan
 ts will be responsible for travel to and from Raleigh and expenses in Rale
 igh during pre- and post-trip sessions. See below for scholarship opportun
 ities.\n\n*The cost of all Institutes are significantly reduced thanks the
  generous support of the Friends of the Museum and the Goodnight Education
 al Foundation. Teachers that apply and are selected from the list of easte
 rn counties (see below for details) may be eligible to receive a Simple Gi
 fts Scholarship\, which is provided through the generous support of the Si
 mple Gifts Fund and the Anonymous Trust. \n \n\nApplications for Mexico’
 s Magical Migrations 2027 Institute are now open. The application deadline
  is Monday\, October 12\, 2026.\n\nAll applications received by the deadli
 ne will be considered equally\, so please do not rush your application! Th
 e selection process for this program is competitive\, so please make sure 
 you take your time and fully complete the application. All applicants must
  have a complete Educator Application and a Supervisor Application. \n\nEd
 ucator Application \n\nSupervisor Application\n\nApplications for Summer 2
 027 Institutes (Yellowstone and Blue Ridge) will open in November 2026.
LOCATION:Toluca\, Macho de Agua\, and Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico and Raleigh\
 , N.C.
SUMMARY:Mexico’s Magical Migrations Institute
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mexicos-magical-migrations-i
 nstitute
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
